{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CableShiftFourfold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CableShiftFourfold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.AlphaShiftOneDimChannel"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sqWritheReadout_not_fourfold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sqWritheReadout_not_fourfold","kind":"theorem","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L273-L287","doc":"**The converse guard.**  Cyclicity is not enough: this cyclic readout scales\nby SIXTEEN under cabling, not four, for any word of nonzero writhe.  So\n`fourfold_of_multiplicative`'s hypothesis is load-bearing — the law is about\nmultiplicativity, and a merely-cyclic readout (which is what every\nhigher-dimensional character is) breaks it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sqWritheReadout_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sqWritheReadout_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L266-L271","doc":"`sqWritheReadout` is cyclic: it takes the same value on `v ++ w` and\n`w ++ v`.  So it has the property every character shares. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sqWritheReadout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sqWritheReadout","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L261-L264","doc":"A readout built from the SQUARE of the writhe.  It is cyclic — the writhe is\ninvariant under cyclic permutation, hence so is its square — but it is not\nmultiplicative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.fourfold_of_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.fourfold_of_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L247-L259","doc":"**The property the law rides on.**  Any readout that is multiplicative on\nconcatenation and sends each letter to `s^{±1}` quadruples under cabling — the\nchannel it came from is irrelevant.  The hypothesis is MULTIPLICATIVITY; see\n`sqWritheReadout_not_fourfold` for why cyclicity would not do. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eq_charOf_of_multiplicative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eq_charOf_of_multiplicative","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L230-L245","doc":"A multiplicative readout is determined by its values on single letters, so\nit agrees with `charOf`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cable_letters_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cable_letters_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L213-L228","doc":"Cabling a word of genuine braid letters produces genuine braid letters:\nevery entry of `cableBlock g` is nonzero when `g` is, since `2g` is even and\nnonzero while `2g ± 1` are odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.charOf_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.charOf_append","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L202-L211","doc":"The character is multiplicative on concatenation — an algebra map into a\ncommutative target.  This is the property, stated on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cable_fails_on_zero_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cable_fails_on_zero_letter","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L166-L171","doc":"**Non-vacuity II.**  The `g ≠ 0` hypothesis is load-bearing, not\ndecorative: a degenerate zero letter produces a block with MIXED signs\n(`[0, -1, 1, 0]`), and the ×4 law fails on it.  Recorded so that a later reader\ndoes not drop the hypothesis as noise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.nonpositive_witness_has_inverse_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.nonpositive_witness_has_inverse_letter","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L162-L164","doc":"The witness word really is non-positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cable_nonpositive_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cable_nonpositive_witness","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L155-L160","doc":"**Non-vacuity I.**  A genuinely non-positive word — `σ₁σ₁σ₂⁻¹`, which\ncontains an inverse letter — still quadruples.  Without this the ×4 law above\ncould be read as a positive-word statement carrying an unused hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cable_deficit_zero_on_oneDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cable_deficit_zero_on_oneDim","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L143-L153","doc":"**(P3, the half that is provable here) The deficit vanishes on a\none-dimensional channel.**  `4·α − α(cable)` is identically zero there, so a\nnonzero deficit forces the maximizing partition to be intermediate.  Which\npartition actually attains the maximum is a measurement, not a theorem — see\nthe module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.val_charOf_cable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.val_charOf_cable","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L133-L141","doc":"**(P2) The cable-shift law on a one-dimensional channel: exactly ×4, for\nevery word.**  This is the derived statement that answers \"what is the law for\na non-positive word?\" — the law is the same one, because a one-dimensional\nchannel cannot tell a non-positive word from a positive one except through its\nwrithe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.charOf_cable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.charOf_cable","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L124-L131","doc":"**The character on a one-dimensional channel is a fourth power.**  Since\nsuch a channel sees only the writhe (`charOf_eq_zpow`) and the writhe\nquadruples, cabling raises the character to the fourth — with no positivity\nhypothesis anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.length_cable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.length_cable","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L113-L122","doc":"The cable of a word has four times its length: the substitution is\nlength-multiplying by the same factor it multiplies the writhe by. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cable","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L98-L111","doc":"**(P1) The writhe quadruples**, for every word — positive, negative or\nmixed.  The only hypothesis is that the letters are genuine braid generators\n(`g ≠ 0`); the substitution never mixes signs within a block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cableBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cableBlock","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L90-L96","doc":"One letter contributes exactly four letters of its own sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cableBlock_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cableBlock_neg","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L82-L88","doc":"Every letter of an inverse letter's block is negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cableBlock_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.writhe_cableBlock_pos","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L74-L80","doc":"Every letter of a positive letter's block is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cable","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L69-L72","doc":"The 2-parallel cable of a braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cableBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cableBlock","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CableShiftFourfold.lean#L59-L67","doc":"The four letters the 2-parallel substitution writes for one letter `g`.\n\nFor `g = i > 0` this is `σ_{2i} σ_{2i−1} σ_{2i+1} σ_{2i}`, the standard\n2-parallel image.  For `g = −i < 0` the image is the block reversed with every\nletter inverted, `σ_{2i}⁻¹ σ_{2i+1}⁻¹ σ_{2i−1}⁻¹ σ_{2i}⁻¹` — which is the SAME\nlist of expressions in `g`, since `−(2i+1) = 2g − 1` and `−(2i−1) = 2g + 1`.\nThat coincidence is why the sign bookkeeping below needs no case split on the\nletter's own sign beyond `g ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}